mary", "oldValue": "Alliance of public service media entities. European Broadcasting Union is a organization in Geneva, established in 1950-02-12. Holds notable historical significance, documented across 66 language editions of Wikipedia. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "The European Broadcasting Union (EBU), established on February 12, 1950, in Geneva, represents a coalition of public service broadcasters across Europe and beyond. With its roots in the post-World War II era, the EBU emerged as a response to the need for cooperative broadcasting and cultural exchange among nations recovering from war. This institution has played a pivotal role in shaping media standards and practices, influencing the broader landscape of public broadcasting and media policy in Europe.

